const mentorMap={
 'Legal register':'A legal register converts the workplace profile into applicable duties, required evidence and compliance status, so the coordinator knows where to start.',
 'HIRARC':'HIRARC should follow the real job sequence. Start from a JMS, involve workers/supervisors, rate the risk, choose controls and track implementation.',
 'CHRA':'The SME can maintain the chemical register and SDS internally, but a formal CHRA requires the appropriate registered assessor. The system should track the assessor’s recommendations to closure.',
 'Noise risk assessment':'Start with in-house noise identification. When the trigger indicates formal assessment, appoint the appropriate assessor and track controls, training and health-surveillance actions.',
 'Safety committee':'The committee is where the system is run month-to-month: review incidents, inspections, HIRARC changes, worker concerns and overdue actions.',
 'Emergency drill':'A drill is not just an event. Record the scenario, timings, observations, failures, actions, owners and evidence of closure.',
 'OSHWA / SOLVE':'Use the recognised maturity pathway rather than inventing an internal score. Link each checkpoint to real evidence and show the weakest element first.'
};
